To refer to the 'bottom-right' anchor of a transformer in Konva, you can use the `top` and `right` properties of the anchor element. Here's how you can do it:

1. **Create an Anchor Element**: First, create an anchor element in your HTML. For example:
   ```html
   <div id="myAnchor"></div>
   ```

2. **Set the `top` and `right` Properties**: Use the `top` and `right` properties to position the anchor at the bottom-right corner of the container. For instance:
   ```html
   <div id="myAnchor" class="myAnchor"></div>
   ```

   Then, you can use the `top` and `right` properties to position the anchor at the bottom-right corner of the container:
   ```html
   <div id="myAnchor" class="myAnchor"></div>
   ```

   ```javascript
   var myAnchor = new Konva.AnaAnchor({
       x: 100, // x-coordinate of the anchor
       y: 100, // y-coordinate of the anchor
       width: 50, // width of the anchor
       height: 50 // height of the anchor
   });

   // Set the anchor to the bottom-right corner
   myAnchor.set({
       top: 100, // Top coordinate of the anchor
       right: 100  // Right coordinate of the anchor
   });
   ```

3. **Display the Anchor**: Finally, you can display the anchor in your Konva view:
   ```html
   <div id="myContainer" class="myContainer"></div>
   ```

   ```javascript
   var myContainer = new Konva.Container({
       children: [
           new Konva.AnaAnchor({
               x: 100, // x-coordinate of the anchor
               y: 100, // y-coordinate of the anchor
               width: 50, // width of the anchor
               height: 50 // height of the anchor
           })
       ]
   });

   // Add the container to the view
   var view = new Konva.View({
       container: myContainer
   });

   // Display the view
   view.show();
   ```

By using the `top` and `right` properties, you can position the anchor at the bottom-right corner of the container, effectively creating a visual effect where the anchor is positioned at the bottom-right corner of the container.
